Menu-loop reloc-applier sites: neutralise the FLAKY (nondeterministic) SIGSEGV that patches 125/126
exposed on the static main menu, keeping native<->wasm bit-identical.

ROOT CAUSE (watchpoint + segv-EIP + pattern-init proven).  Patches 125/126 advanced execution into the
main MENU LOOP (FUN_0000_00d0: while (FUN_1000_5c5f(), !stop) { FUN_1000_5c3a(); FUN_0000_cae6(); }).
FUN_1000_5c3a installs method-vector reloc sections via  xor bx,bx; mov si,0xNNN; lcall [DGROUP:0x12]
(the FAR applier FUN_0000_f842); FUN_1000_5c5f clears them via lcall [DGROUP:0x16] (f860->f869);
FUN_1000_2ebe installs si=0x1b8 the same way.  Ghidra dropped the BX/SI section operands at the indirect
call site AND the x86 string-op segment bases inside f842/f860/f869, so the raw (*[c012])()/(*[c016])()
far-calls ran the base-lost C bodies on UNINITIALISED register-arg garbage: f842  if (param_1!=0) { uVar1
= *param_3; ... }  dereferences the wild param_3 host pointer whenever the garbage BX is nonzero ->
FLAKY SIGSEGV (~30-40%, segv EIP = FUN_0000_f842).

FIX.  The applier CANNOT be routed to a faithful install here: the install has no observable effect on the
static menu (native AND wasm render the byte-exact menu, AE=0 vs the DOSBox reference, WITHOUT it) but it
diverges execution under the wasm cooperative time base (wasm starves at a pre-menu frame while native
reaches the menu -> native != wasm).  So the deterministic, dual-target-identical behaviour is the inert
one every non-crashing run already produced: elide the base-lost applier calls (same class as patch 053s
elision of the bx==0 no-op reloc apply).  2ebe + the three 5c3a installs + the three 5c5f clears are
elided; 5c5fs two installed-handler far-calls [0x1696]/[0x169e] are kept (they trap to a safe no-op while
uninstalled).  Deferred: the faithful vtable install + a cooperative pump for the spin-wait it enables is
sub-screen frontier work.
